en c = 0. beta is defined as m/R_c with R_c = 1/sqrt(c), which diverges at c = 0, so the arm cannot be constructed from the specification. It must state explicitly that R_c is the fixed constant 1 (not 1/sqrt(c)) and that beta is inherited frozen from the c = 1 epoch-0 step-0 calibration (or give an explicit c = 0 calibration rule)."], "tests": [{"finding": "rho normalisation/population changed from n_train - 1 over all training items (range [0,(n_pos-1)/(n_train-1)]) to n_pos - 1 over S (range claimed [0,1]).", "eval_id": "rho_denominator_must_be_n_train_minus_1", "code": "def check(spec):
